This repository contains a new Rust implementation of Markitai's public
conversion interfaces. Project source is licensed under MIT; see LICENSE.
The standard license text and original project attribution are retained.

Document parsers and runtime dependencies are resolved in Cargo.lock. The
initial implementation uses anydoc, pdf-inspector, scraper/html5ever, htmd,
mail-parser, reqwest/rustls, and other Rust crates under their respective
licenses. It does not bundle or invoke the reference Python PDF engine.

Before distributing a release, generate the resolved dependency inventory
and include each dependency's applicable license/copyright notices. A crate's
metadata license identifier alone is not the complete notice bundle.
Reference test fixtures remain in the reference checkout; audit reports record
fixture hashes and never redistribute them as newly authored fixtures.

The embedded browser workspace includes Marked 18.0.14 (MIT), DOMPurify
3.4.16 (Apache-2.0), Preact 10.29.8 (MIT), icon path data from Phosphor Icons
2.1.10 (MIT) and the Inter 5.3.0 variable font (SIL Open Font License 1.1).
Their complete notices are in vendor/web/marked-LICENSE,
vendor/web/DOMPurify-LICENSE, vendor/web/preact-LICENSE,
vendor/web/phosphor-LICENSE and vendor/web/Inter-OFL.txt. Download provenance,
upstream package integrity and embedded-file hashes are recorded in
vendor/web/provenance.json.

Windows and Linux builds render PDF pages with hayro 0.7.1 (MIT/Apache-2.0),
which embeds the Foxit standard-14 substitute fonts from PDFium (BSD-3-Clause),
Adobe's predefined CMaps (BSD-3-Clause) and a CC0 CMYK profile; their notices
are in licenses/hayro/.

Windows and Linux builds decode AVIF with rav1d (BSD-2-Clause; VideoLAN, the
dav1d authors and the Internet Security Research Group), vendored from upstream
commit d3d1cd67 in vendor/rav1d with the changes listed in
vendor/rav1d/MARKITAI-PATCH.md. Its Rust API derives from dav1d-rs (MIT,
Luca Barbato); both notices are in vendor/rav1d/COPYING and
vendor/rav1d/LICENSE-dav1d-rs.

The Numbers reader uses iwork 0.2.1 (MIT), pinned in Cargo.lock. Its independently
sourced regression documents are from numbers-parser (MIT), with the original
license and exact source identities in
crates/markitai-core/src/formats/numbers/fixtures/.

The bounded offline token-pricing catalog derives selected rows from LiteLLM
1.106.0.dev2's bundled model data. Its original BerriAI copyright/license notice,
exact selected source objects and official tariff/alias provenance are retained
in licenses/pricing/. This attribution does not assert universal price coverage
or complete legal review of the dependency bundle.

Reviewed supplemental upstream dependency notices and full terms are included in
licenses/upstream/. The unmodified MPL-covered selectors 0.38.0 source is available
offline at licenses/upstream/source-archives/selectors-0.38.0.crate; its exact
checksum, upstream download URL and license are recorded in that directory.
These paths are relative to the archive's attribution root (the Python wheel
uses its .dist-info/licenses/ directory). Three historical objc2-family MIT
notices remain explicitly review-needed. This collection does not complete a
legal review or resolve the upstream Apple SDK licensing discussion.

The restricted Codex model capability catalog derives from OpenAI Codex
rust-v0.159.0 (Apache-2.0). The complete original license/copyright notice,
modified catalog, change description and exact source identities are included in
licenses/codex/. Only gpt-5.5 is retained and apply_patch_tool_type is set to null;
the official runtime executable is not modified or bundled by this adapter.
